  "metaDescription": "Government officials and labor leaders demand accountability as search and rescue teams continue to recover victims from the Cikande factory fire site.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "Government ministries and labor advisors have launched investigations into the fatal factory fire in Cikande, Banten, to determine the cause.",
    "Search and rescue operations are ongoing at the site, with 26 remains recovered so far and dozens of individuals still reported as missing.",
    "Officials and labor representatives are focusing on potential health and safety standard violations while providing support to affected families."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "A major fire broke out at the PT Fonusa Agung Mulia candy factory in the Pancatama Industrial Estate, Cikande, Serang, on November 21, 2026. Following the incident, the Ministry of Manpower, the Ministry of Industry, and labor advisors have initiated investigations into the tragedy, which is currently suspected to have been caused by an electrical short circuit in an air conditioning unit. As recovery efforts enter their third day, search teams are focusing on a 2,000-square-meter area of the debris. Families of the missing workers have begun submitting ante-mortem data to assist with the identification of victims as the death toll rises. In response, government officials have called for a rigorous evaluation of workplace health and safety compliance across industrial sectors to prevent future occurrences, while labor leaders have formally requested that the company management take full responsibility for the incident.",
